"[0806.4976v2] Geometry of configuration spaces of tensegrities (https://arxiv.org/abs/0806.4976v2)\nciteturn1339view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/0806.4976v2\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Combinatorics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 30 Jun 2008 (【5†v1】), last revised 30 Jun 2008 (this version, v2)]\nL9: # Title:Geometry of configuration spaces of tensegrities\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【6†Franck Doray】, 【7†Oleg Karpenkov】, 【8†Jan Schepers】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Geometry of configuration spaces of tensegrities, by Franck Doray and 2 other authors\nL14: \nL15: 【9†View PDF】 【10†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract: Consider a graph G with n vertices. In this paper we study geometric conditions for an n-tuple of points in R^d to admit a tensegrity with underlying graph G. We introduce and investigate a natural stratification, depending on G, of the configuration space of all n-tuples in R^d. In particular we find surgeries on graphs that give relations between different strata.\nL17: Based on numerous examples we give a description of geometric conditions defining the strata for plane tensegrities, we conjecture that the list of such conditions is sufficient to describe any stratum. We conclude the paper with particular examples of strata for tensegrities in the plane with a small number of vertices.\nL18: Subjects:  | Combinatorics (math.CO); Metric Geometry (math.MG)\nL19: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 52C30, 05C10\nL20: Cite as:  | 【11†arXiv:0806.4976】 [math.CO]\nL21:    | (or 【12†arXiv:0806.4976v2】 [math.CO] for this version)\nL22:    | 【13†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.0806.4976†doi.org】 arXiv-is